WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.600
Goal: understand how the British constitution works (not codified in a single text) without confusing university-level analysis with the official test.

2
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:24.700
The United Kingdom combines Acts of Parliament (Statute Law), judge-made law (Common Law) and constitutional conventions (e.g. the Prime Minister must have the confidence of the House of Commons).

3
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:40.300
Strict separation: the official Life in the UK test is booked only on GOV.UK (24 questions, 45 minutes). This block broadens historical and institutional knowledge, inspired by themes from Oxford History & Politics, without university endorsement.

4
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:47.500
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
